        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Rhodochrosite is a manganese carbonate, raspberry pink to cherry red. It mainly forms in low- to moderate-temperature hydrothermal veins associated with silver, lead, zinc and copper deposits, where manganese-rich fluids precipitate late in crystallisation, often with fluorite, quartz and pyrite. In some deposits it is also deposited as a secondary mineral, in stalactites and concentric layers: this is the famous “Inca rose” of Argentina, with pink and white bands.",
